 </subquestions>
 <question_l10ns>
  <fields>
   <fieldname>id</fieldname>
   <fieldname>qid</fieldname>
   <fieldname>question</fieldname>
   <fieldname>help</fieldname>
   <fieldname>script</fieldname>
   <fieldname>language</fieldname>
  </fields>
  <rows>
   <row>
    <id>1</id>
    <qid>1010001</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perception and beliefs about the mind — a short survey&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Conducted by the Alpine Institute for Advanced Research. Principal investigator: Matthias Gruber, research@matthiasgruber.com.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is this about?&lt;/strong&gt; We study how ordinary perceptual experiences relate to people's views about the mind. To keep the results unbiased, we will explain the exact question once data collection has closed; the explanation will then be posted at &lt;a href="https://alpine-institute.eu/study/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://alpine-institute.eu/study/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I do?&lt;/strong&gt; Answer questions online for about 25 minutes: about you (age band and gender only, no names), everyday perceptual experiences, your views about the mind, and a few standard personality and experience questionnaires. Some questions concern unusual experiences (for example, hearing things while falling asleep) or thoughts about death. You can skip any question.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Is it voluntary?&lt;/strong&gt; Yes. Nobody — including your employer and the researchers — will know whether you took part. Taking part or not has no consequences of any kind. You can stop at any time. Pages you have already completed are saved anonymously as you go, but incomplete responses are never analysed and are deleted when data collection closes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Is it anonymous?&lt;/strong&gt; We do not collect your name, email, IP address or any device identifier in this survey. Answers are reported only in summaries. We ask only for a coarse age band and gender, so that no combination of answers points to a person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional second part.&lt;/strong&gt; At the end we ask whether we may contact you for a second session. If you agree, a separate form asks for your email address. It is stored separately, cannot be linked to your answers, is used only to send that invitation, and is deleted when recruitment ends (at the latest after 12 months).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risks and benefits.&lt;/strong&gt; No risks beyond everyday life are expected. If any question troubles you, you can contact Matthias Gruber, research@matthiasgruber.com; in acute distress: Telefonseelsorge 142 (Austria), Die Dargebotene Hand 143 (Switzerland, Liechtenstein). There is no payment; you contribute to basic research on consciousness, and you will receive the summary of results on the Institute website.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data protection.&lt;/strong&gt; Controller: Matthias Gruber, research@matthiasgruber.com. The survey is hosted by the Alpine Institute for Advanced Research as processor. Full privacy notice: &lt;a href="https://alpine-institute.eu/study/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://alpine-institute.eu/study/privacy/&lt;/a&gt;. We treat your survey answers as anonymous: the survey stores no name, email, IP address or date, and published data are coarsened so that no answer can be traced to you. Some questions touch on religious and philosophical beliefs and on health; where the GDPR applies, the legal basis is your explicit consent (Art. 6(1)(a) and Art. 9(2)(a) GDPR), which you give by ticking the box below. The email address you may give in the separate part-two form is personal data; the legal basis there is also your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). The survey site sets only two technical cookies, a session cookie and a security token against forged form submissions; there is no tracking, no analytics and no third-party content. Data are stored on servers in the EU (self-hosted at survey.alpine-institute.eu); survey answers are kept for 10 years under good scientific practice, and published only in de-identified form (free-text answers are never published). Because nobody can tell which answers are yours, they cannot be withdrawn after you submit them. You may complain to the Austrian Data Protection Authority (dsb.gv.at).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethics.&lt;/strong&gt; The study is anonymous and involves no intervention; under Austrian law it does not require review by an ethics committee.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Questions?&lt;/strong&gt; research@matthiasgruber.com&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>2</id>
    <qid>1010002</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do you agree to take part?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>3</id>
    <qid>1010003</qid>
    <question>Recruitment channel (URL parameter)</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>4</id>
    <qid>1010004</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your interest. You have chosen not to take part, so no further questions will be asked. Please click “Submit” to close the survey, or simply close this window.&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>5</id>
    <qid>1010005</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Your age&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>6</id>
    <qid>1010006</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Your gender&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>7</id>
    <qid>1010007</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How familiar are you with philosophy of mind (e.g. the mind–body problem)?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>8</id>
    <qid>1010008</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Have you ever taken a course or read a book on consciousness or philosophy of mind?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>9</id>
    <qid>1010009</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Before today, had you heard of the 'hard problem of consciousness'?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>10</id>
    <qid>1010010</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Do you meditate or practise a similar mental technique?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>11</id>
    <qid>1010011</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;If yes, for how many years in total?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>12</id>
    <qid>1010012</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Over the past month, how would you rate your sleep quality overall?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>13</id>
    <qid>1010013</qid>
    <question>{1}</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>14</id>
    <qid>1010014</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;A quick demonstration before the questions. Close your left eye and look at the cross with your right eye. Move closer to or further from the screen slowly. At some distance the dot disappears — that is your blind spot. Now do the same with the second picture: at that distance the gap in the line disappears too. On a phone, turn it sideways first; the demonstration works best on a computer screen.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="aiw343-demo"&gt;&lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 800 380" style="max-width:100%;height:auto" role="img" aria-label="Blind-spot demonstration: a cross on the left and a dot on the right; below, a cross and a horizontal line with a gap at the dot's position."&gt;
  &lt;rect width="800" height="380" fill="#ffffff"/&gt;
  
  &lt;g stroke="#111111" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"&gt;
    &lt;line x1="100" y1="70" x2="100" y2="130"/&gt;
    &lt;line x1="70" y1="100" x2="130" y2="100"/&gt;
  &lt;/g&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="520" cy="100" r="22" fill="#111111"/&gt;
  &lt;text x="400" y="175" font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="20" fill="#444444" text-anchor="middle"&gt;1 — the dot disappears at some distance&lt;/text&gt;
  
  &lt;g stroke="#111111" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"&gt;
    &lt;line x1="100" y1="230" x2="100" y2="290"/&gt;
    &lt;line x1="70" y1="260" x2="130" y2="260"/&gt;
  &lt;/g&gt;
  &lt;g stroke="#1f5fbf" stroke-width="10"&gt;
    &lt;line x1="300" y1="260" x2="492" y2="260"/&gt;
    &lt;line x1="548" y1="260" x2="740" y2="260"/&gt;
  &lt;/g&gt;
  &lt;text x="400" y="335" font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="20" fill="#444444" text-anchor="middle"&gt;2 — at the same distance the gap closes: the line looks unbroken&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>15</id>
    <qid>1010015</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Did the dot disappear?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>16</id>
    <qid>1010016</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How often have you experienced the following in the past 12 months? There are no right or wrong answers — many of these are common.&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>17</id>
    <qid>1010017</qid>
    <question>With my eyes closed, I see flickering, dots, or patterns of light or colour.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>18</id>
    <qid>1010018</qid>
    <question>Rubbing or pressing on my closed eyes produces lights or patterns.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>19</id>
    <qid>1010019</qid>
    <question>In ordinary daylight I see a fine, flickering "static", like an old TV screen, over everything I look at.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>20</id>
    <qid>1010020</qid>
    <question>After looking at something bright, an afterimage stays in my view or gets in the way of what I am looking at.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>21</id>
    <qid>1010021</qid>
    <question>I notice blurred, missing or "filled-in" patches in what I see that turn out not to match what is really there.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>22</id>
    <qid>1010022</qid>
    <question>While falling asleep, I see images, faces or scenes that I did not intend to imagine.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>23</id>
    <qid>1010023</qid>
    <question>While falling asleep or waking up, I hear sounds, voices or my name when nothing is there.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>24</id>
    <qid>1010024</qid>
    <question>In silence I hear ringing, hissing or faint music that has no outside source.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>25</id>
    <qid>1010025</qid>
    <question>When I stare at one point, parts of what I am looking at fade out or disappear.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>26</id>
    <qid>1010026</qid>
    <question>Words, faces or objects seem to assemble themselves a moment late, as if I could watch them being put together.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>27</id>
    <qid>1010027</qid>
    <question>A word or thought seems to arrive in my mind just before I have "thought" it.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>28</id>
    <qid>1010028</qid>
    <question>When dozing off, my body suddenly jerks or I feel I am falling.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>29</id>
    <qid>1010029</qid>
    <question>In dim light I see shapes or movement at the edge of my vision that turn out to be nothing.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>30</id>
    <qid>1010030</qid>
    <question>A word I repeat or stare at loses its meaning and turns into mere sound or marks.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>31</id>
    <qid>1010031</qid>
    <question>I have seen a person who was five metres tall.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>32</id>
    <qid>1010032</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Has a doctor ever diagnosed you with…&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>33</id>
    <qid>1010033</qid>
    <question>migraine with aura</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>34</id>
    <qid>1010034</qid>
    <question>visual snow syndrome</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>35</id>
    <qid>1010035</qid>
    <question>tinnitus</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>36</id>
    <qid>1010036</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Do you currently take medication that you know affects perception or sleep?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>37</id>
    <qid>1010037</qid>
    <question>{if(is_empty(blockorder.NAOK), if(is_empty(pliseen.NAOK), "B", "A"), blockorder.NAOK)}</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>38</id>
    <qid>1010038</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How well do the following statements describe your personality? I see myself as someone who …&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>39</id>
    <qid>1010039</qid>
    <question>… is reserved</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>40</id>
    <qid>1010040</qid>
    <question>… is generally trusting</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>41</id>
    <qid>1010041</qid>
    <question>… tends to be lazy</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>42</id>
    <qid>1010042</qid>
    <question>… is relaxed, handles stress well</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>43</id>
    <qid>1010043</qid>
    <question>… has few artistic interests</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>44</id>
    <qid>1010044</qid>
    <question>… is outgoing, sociable</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>45</id>
    <qid>1010045</qid>
    <question>To show that you are reading, please select "disagree a little" for this line.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>46</id>
    <qid>1010046</qid>
    <question>… tends to find fault with others</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>47</id>
    <qid>1010047</qid>
    <question>… does a thorough job</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>48</id>
    <qid>1010048</qid>
    <question>… gets nervous easily</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>49</id>
    <qid>1010049</qid>
    <question>… has an active imagination</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>50</id>
    <qid>1010050</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How much do you agree with each statement?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>51</id>
    <qid>1010051</qid>
    <question>When I pay close attention to my own mind, I sense that far more is going on than I can ever reach.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>52</id>
    <qid>1010052</qid>
    <question>I have the impression that most of what makes up my mind is hidden from me, yet not entirely out of sight.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>53</id>
    <qid>1010053</qid>
    <question>My experience seems to rest on something vast that operates just beyond the edge of what I can notice.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>54</id>
    <qid>1010054</qid>
    <question>My mind has depths that introspection can hint at but never reach.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>55</id>
    <qid>1010055</qid>
    <question>When I look inward, what I find is all there is to my mind.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>56</id>
    <qid>1010056</qid>
    <question>There is much more to my own mind than I will ever be able to know from the inside.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>57</id>
    <qid>1010057</qid>
    <question>Even a complete scientific account of the brain would leave out what it is like to experience something.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>58</id>
    <qid>1010058</qid>
    <question>Science will one day fully explain how conscious experience arises from the brain.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>59</id>
    <qid>1010059</qid>
    <question>What it is like to see red cannot, even in principle, be captured by physical facts.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>60</id>
    <qid>1010060</qid>
    <question>Knowing every physical fact about a person's brain would tell you exactly what they are experiencing.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>61</id>
    <qid>1010061</qid>
    <question>Science could one day fully explain the following phenomenon: perceiving colour.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>62</id>
    <qid>1010062</qid>
    <question>Science could one day fully explain the following phenomenon: feeling pain.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>63</id>
    <qid>1010063</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How much do you agree with each statement?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>64</id>
    <qid>1010064</qid>
    <question>Minds are in principle independent of bodies, to which they are only temporarily attached.ᵃ</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>65</id>
    <qid>1010065</qid>
    <question>The mind is a special form of energy, currently unknown to man, that is in contact with the brain and affects it.ᵃ</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>66</id>
    <qid>1010066</qid>
    <question>Thought processes cannot be just brain processes.ᵃ</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>67</id>
    <qid>1010067</qid>
    <question>The mind is immaterial and it works with the brain to generate our behavior.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>68</id>
    <qid>1010068</qid>
    <question>The consciousness of myself does not die with my physical body.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>69</id>
    <qid>1010069</qid>
    <question>The body belongs to the world of material and natural laws. The mind is a different kind of existence a spiritual way of being.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>70</id>
    <qid>1010070</qid>
    <question>The body is material and the mind is immaterial.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>71</id>
    <qid>1010071</qid>
    <question>Some mental processes have no connection to brain processes.ᵃ</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>72</id>
    <qid>1010072</qid>
    <question>The mind is not part of the brain, but it affects the brain.ᵃ</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>73</id>
    <qid>1010073</qid>
    <question>Mental states are activities of my nervous system.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>74</id>
    <qid>1010074</qid>
    <question>The mind as a whole is made up of substance and material processes.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>75</id>
    <qid>1010075</qid>
    <question>The mind and the brain are totally different things.ᵃ</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>76</id>
    <qid>1010076</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How much do you agree with each statement?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>77</id>
    <qid>1010077</qid>
    <question>The human being is composed of two realities, one physical (the body) and one mental, which somehow interact</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>78</id>
    <qid>1010078</qid>
    <question>All mental activity (thoughts, feelings, etc.) of the human being is reducible to the functioning of the brain</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>79</id>
    <qid>1010079</qid>
    <question>The human being is a unitary reality, but mental activity is not entirely reducible to the functioning of the nervous system</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>80</id>
    <qid>1010080</qid>
    <question>The human being is a unity with two dimensions, one mental and one biological, which are distinct but inseparable</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>81</id>
    <qid>1010081</qid>
    <question>The human being is a set of functions that could be implemented in different physical substrates</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>82</id>
    <qid>1010082</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How much do you agree with each statement?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>83</id>
    <qid>1010083</qid>
    <question>The soul continues to exist though the body may die.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>84</id>
    <qid>1010084</qid>
    <question>Some individuals are able to levitate (lift) objects through mental forces.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>85</id>
    <qid>1010085</qid>
    <question>Black magic really exists.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>86</id>
    <qid>1010086</qid>
    <question>Black cats can bring bad luck.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>87</id>
    <qid>1010087</qid>
    <question>Your mind or soul can leave your body and travel (astral projection).</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>88</id>
    <qid>1010088</qid>
    <question>The abominable snowman of Tibet exists.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>89</id>
    <qid>1010089</qid>
    <question>Astrology is a way to accurately predict the future.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>90</id>
    <qid>1010090</qid>
    <question>There is a devil.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>91</id>
    <qid>1010091</qid>
    <question>Psychokinesis, the movement of objects through psychic powers, does exist.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>92</id>
    <qid>1010092</qid>
    <question>Witches do exist.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>93</id>
    <qid>1010093</qid>
    <question>If you break a mirror, you will have bad luck.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>94</id>
    <qid>1010094</qid>
    <question>During altered states, such as sleep or trances, the spirit can leave the body.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>95</id>
    <qid>1010095</qid>
    <question>The Loch Ness monster of Scotland exists.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>96</id>
    <qid>1010096</qid>
    <question>The horoscope accurately tells a person’s future.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>97</id>
    <qid>1010097</qid>
    <question>I believe in God</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>98</id>
    <qid>1010098</qid>
    <question>A person’s thoughts can influence the movement of a physical object.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>99</id>
    <qid>1010099</qid>
    <question>Through the use of formulas and incantations, it is possible to cast spells on persons.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>100</id>
    <qid>1010100</qid>
    <question>The number “13” is unlucky.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>101</id>
    <qid>1010101</qid>
    <question>Reincarnation does occur.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>102</id>
    <qid>1010102</qid>
    <question>There is life on other planets.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>103</id>
    <qid>1010103</qid>
    <question>Some psychics can accurately predict the future.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>104</id>
    <qid>1010104</qid>
    <question>There is a heaven and a hell.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>105</id>
    <qid>1010105</qid>
    <question>Mind reading is not possible.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>106</id>
    <qid>1010106</qid>
    <question>There are actual cases of witchcraft.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>107</id>
    <qid>1010107</qid>
    <question>It is possible to communicate with the dead.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>108</id>
    <qid>1010108</qid>
    <question>Some people have an unexplained ability to predict the future.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>109</id>
    <qid>1010109</qid>
    <question>I have never in my life used a telephone of any kind.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>110</id>
    <qid>1010110</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How religious or spiritual are you?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>111</id>
    <qid>1010111</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How often do you attend religious services or practise religious rituals?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>112</id>
    <qid>1010112</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Some questions concern unusual experiences or thoughts about death. You can skip any question. If anything here troubles you, the contact at the end of the survey can point you to support.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>113</id>
    <qid>1010113</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Please answer each question with yes or no.&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>114</id>
    <qid>1010114</qid>
    <question>Do you ever have a sense of vague danger or sudden dread for reasons that you do not understand?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>115</id>
    <qid>1010115</qid>
    <question>When in the dark do you often see shapes and forms even though there is nothing there?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>116</id>
    <qid>1010116</qid>
    <question>Are your thoughts sometimes so strong that you can almost hear them?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>117</id>
    <qid>1010117</qid>
    <question>Have you ever thought that you had special, almost magical powers?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>118</id>
    <qid>1010118</qid>
    <question>Have you sometimes sensed an evil presence around you, even though you could not see it?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>119</id>
    <qid>1010119</qid>
    <question>Do you think that you could learn to read other's minds if you wanted to?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>120</id>
    <qid>1010120</qid>
    <question>When you look in the mirror does your face sometimes seem quite different from usual?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>121</id>
    <qid>1010121</qid>
    <question>Do ideas and insights sometimes come to you so fast that you cannot express them all?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>122</id>
    <qid>1010122</qid>
    <question>Can some people make you aware of them just by thinking about you?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>123</id>
    <qid>1010123</qid>
    <question>Does a passing thought ever seem so real it frightens you?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>124</id>
    <qid>1010124</qid>
    <question>Do you feel that your accidents are caused by mysterious forces?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>125</id>
    <qid>1010125</qid>
    <question>Does your sense of smell sometimes become unusually strong?</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>126</id>
    <qid>1010126</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How often have you had the following experiences in the past 12 months, when you were not under the influence of alcohol or drugs?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>127</id>
    <qid>1010127</qid>
    <question>I find myself staring into space and thinking of nothing.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>128</id>
    <qid>1010128</qid>
    <question>People, objects, or the world around me seem strange or unreal.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>129</id>
    <qid>1010129</qid>
    <question>I find that I did things that I do not remember doing.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>130</id>
    <qid>1010130</qid>
    <question>When I am alone, I talk out loud to myself.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>131</id>
    <qid>1010131</qid>
    <question>I feel as though I were looking at the world through a fog so that people and things seem far away or unclear.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>132</id>
    <qid>1010132</qid>
    <question>I am able to ignore pain.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>133</id>
    <qid>1010133</qid>
    <question>I act so differently from one situation to another that it is almost as if I were two different people.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>134</id>
    <qid>1010134</qid>
    <question>I can do things very easily that would usually be hard for me.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>135</id>
    <qid>1010135</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;How much do you agree with each statement?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>136</id>
    <qid>1010136</qid>
    <question>Death is no doubt a grim experience.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>137</id>
    <qid>1010137</qid>
    <question>The prospect of my own death arouses anxiety in me.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>138</id>
    <qid>1010138</qid>
    <question>I am disturbed by the finality of death.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>139</id>
    <qid>1010139</qid>
    <question>I have an intense fear of death.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>140</id>
    <qid>1010140</qid>
    <question>The subject of life after death troubles me greatly.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>141</id>
    <qid>1010141</qid>
    <question>The fact that death will mean the end of everything as I know it frightens me.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>142</id>
    <qid>1010142</qid>
    <question>The uncertainty of not knowing what happens after death worries me.</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>143</id>
    <qid>1010143</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;What do you think this survey was about?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>144</id>
    <qid>1010144</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Did you have a hypothesis about what the researchers expect? If so, what?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>145</id>
    <qid>1010145</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Did you notice any connection between different parts of the survey? If so, which?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>146</id>
    <qid>1010146</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;Anything else you'd like to tell us?&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>147</id>
    <qid>1010147</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Thank you — your answers have been saved.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are planning a second, separate part: a session of about 45 minutes (online or on site) with a short perception task and a brief eyes-closed relaxation exercise.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>148</id>
    <qid>1010148</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;May we contact you to invite you to part two?&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Your answers above stay anonymous. If you say yes, a separate form opens that asks only for your email address. That form is stored apart from this survey and cannot be connected to your answers. Saying yes commits you to nothing; you can decline the invitation later.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id>149</id>
    <qid>1010149</qid>
    <question>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://survey.alpine-institute.eu/index.php/343102?lang=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Open the contact form for part two (opens in a new tab)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</question>
    <language>en</language>
   </row>
  </rows>
 </question_l10ns>
