                                                }
                                                &lt;/style&gt;Hello,&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;A new response was submitted for your survey '{SURVEYNAME}'.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Click the following link to reload the survey:&lt;br /&gt;{RELOADURL}&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Click the following link to see the individual response:&lt;br /&gt;{VIEWRESPONSEURL}&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Click the following link to edit the individual response:&lt;br /&gt;{EDITRESPONSEURL}&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;View statistics by clicking here:&lt;br /&gt;{STATISTICSURL}&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;The following answers were given by the participant:&lt;br /&gt;{ANSWERTABLE}</email_admin_responses>
    <surveyls_numberformat>0</surveyls_numberformat>
    <surveyls_language>en</surveyls_language>
    <surveyls_title>Perception and beliefs about the mind — a short survey</surveyls_title>
    <surveyls_endtext>&lt;p&gt;Thank you for taking part.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We will explain the question behind this survey once data collection has closed; the full explanation will then be posted at &lt;a href="https://alpine-institute.eu/study/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;alpine-institute.eu/study&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Many of your colleagues may still take part. Please don't discuss the questions with them until the survey has closed (15 December 2026) — it would distort the results.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Support: Matthias Gruber, research@matthiasgruber.com; in acute distress: Telefonseelsorge 142 (Austria), Die Dargebotene Hand 143 (Switzerland, Liechtenstein)&lt;br /&gt;Principal investigator: Matthias Gruber, research@matthiasgruber.com&lt;br /&gt;Ethics: The study is anonymous and involves no intervention; under Austrian law it does not require review by an ethics committee.&lt;/p&gt;</surveyls_endtext>
